====================================================

QUALITY RULES

====================================================

Do NOT merely summarize.

Do NOT merely list citations.

Do NOT merely list rabbis.

Instead reconstruct the reasoning process.

Treat every verse as a miniature commentary problem.

For every source explain

• what the source originally says

• what words the Gemara notices

• what words are ignored

• what assumptions are introduced

• which rabbi introduces those assumptions

• whether another rabbi accepts them

• whether another rabbi rejects them

• how the interpretation develops

• how the interpretation advances the argument

• how the interpretation advances the overall sugya

====================================================

TEXTUAL FOCUS

====================================================

When the source is from Tanakh,

pay special attention to the Hebrew.

Explain

• lexical choices

• grammatical forms

• unusual wording

• ambiguity

• repeated words

• omissions

• additions

• syntactic structure

• alternative possible readings

Describe how the Sages transform the plain meaning of the Hebrew text into the interpretation used by the Gemara.

====================================================

FINAL REVIEW

====================================================

After completing every sugya,

perform one final review.

Verify that

Every source has been analyzed.

Every rabbi has been connected to the correct source.

Every interpretation explains the textual reasoning.

Every interpretation explains the Hebrew.

Every source explains how it contributes to the argument.

Every source explains how it contributes to the sugya.

Every sugya contains a complete sugya-level analysis.

Only after this review produce the final JSON.

The final output MUST be valid JSON only.
